 "notes": "ADMX Gen2 haloscope, 90% CL upper limit on |g_agamma| over axion mass 2.669-2.803 ueV (645-680 MHz). Headline curve is the red \"Maxwellian\" line in Fig.4 (limit_plot.pdf in e-print) = boosted Maxwell-Boltzmann lineshape from the isothermal halo model (the paper presents this as its main result; a blue N-Body-lineshape line lies slightly below). Extracted from the vector limit_plot.pdf: figure is rotated 90deg; calibrated linearly from axis tick labels (mass 2.65-2.9 ueV -> page-y; coupling axis 0-18 in 1e-16 GeV^-1 -> page-x, both cross-checked on multiple ticks). The per-frequency limit is very noisy; reported values are medians in 80 equal mass bins of the plotted red polyline, converted to GeV^-1 (x1e-16) and eV (x1e-6). Density 0.45 GeV/cm^3 assumed by paper (Eq.1). Gray vertical veto region 660.16-660.27 MHz (RF interference) is spanned by the interpolation. This limit excludes DFSZ axions assuming 100% dark matter.",
